I agree with gejyspa's disagreement.

{ni'o ta'o}, in gejyspa's example, which color scheme is used is left
ambiguous, to be specified with {mu'a} {ma'i la'oi .RGB.} (is {ma'i} the
right modal?)

{no'i ta'o nai}

My complaint wasn't with the vagueness of the definition of "red" or of
colors in general, but with the sparseness of the directed graph connecting
lojban gismu.

A definition of "red" involving color schemes would make this worse, not
better.

